  "answer_text": "Here is a list of the **best free online auto repair estimate tools** you can use right now:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 1. **RepairPal** \u2014 [repairpal.com/estimator](https://repairpal.com/estimator)\nRepairPal has been the #1 automotive industry estimator since 2008, developed by ASE-certified mechanics. The RepairPal Fair Price Estimator\u2122 is trusted by millions of consumers and over 3,800 RepairPal Certified locations. If the repair cost exceeds the estimate range, they can intervene to work with the shop on your behalf, and the shop agrees to honor the RepairPal Price Guarantee for 30 days after the repair is performed.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 2. **Kelley Blue Book (KBB)** \u2014 [kbb.com/auto-repair](https://www.kbb.com/auto-repair/)\nKBB offers a free car repair estimator to help you find out what you should expect to pay for common auto repairs and maintenance. Estimating repair costs using their tool is considered the best and easiest way to know how much you can expect to pay, based on what others have paid.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 3. **YourMechanic** \u2014 [yourmechanic.com/estimates](https://www.yourmechanic.com/estimates)\nYourMechanic lets you know the cost of your car repair fast and free, with over 600,000 car repair estimates provided since 2012 \u2014 just fill out the form and get your estimate immediately. Their flat-rate pricing is based on the labor time and parts required to fix your car, and estimates show the full price breakdown so there's never any mystery behind service prices. They offer over 600 repair, maintenance, and diagnostic services backed by a 12-month, 12,000-mile warranty.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 4. **AAA** \u2014 [aaa.com/autorepair/estimate](https://www.aaa.com/autorepair/estimate)\nWhether the job involves routine maintenance or more involved repairs, AAA can provide you with an estimate of the cost, including breakdowns for parts, labor, and the member discount available at AAA Approved Auto Repair facilities. Each of the more than 7,000 auto repair shops in the AAA network undergoes a comprehensive investigation and meets AAA's stringent standards.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 5. **NAPA Auto Care** \u2014 [napaonline.com/en/auto-care/car-repair-estimator](https://www.napaonline.com/en/auto-care/car-repair-estimator)\nThe NAPA Auto Care Repair Estimator is a quick and easy way to get price estimates for the most common car repairs and routine maintenance services for your exact make and model.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 6. **Openbay** \u2014 [app.openbay.com](https://app.openbay.com)\nOpenbay comes at no cost with no hidden charges or fees \u2014 it's free to register and use. You can search your car issue and ZIP code to get quotes from top-rated auto repair professionals near you, then compare pricing and book your appointment online.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 7. **Otto** *(Best for Auto Body/Collision)* \u2014 [ottofixit.com](https://www.ottofixit.com)\nOtto's car damage calculator uses AI to analyze a photo of your car and return a free repair estimate in under 30 seconds \u2014 you simply upload a photo, enter your ZIP, and the calculator estimates your repair cost based on thousands of real shop invoices. Otto can provide estimates for auto body damage including dents, scratches, collision repair, and paint damage.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd27 8. **Maaco** *(Best for Body & Paint)* \u2014 [maaco.com/online-estimator](https://www.maaco.com/online-estimator/)\nMaaco offers a free online estimate for auto body repair, painting, and collision repair services.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Pro Tips:\n- Find out what other repair shops will charge for the same work and weigh the costs carefully.\n- If it's a common repair or maintenance item, like an oil change, new brakes, or a tune-up, you can often find a promotion or coupon.\n- The best way to keep your car repair costs low is to keep up with regular maintenance on your vehicle.",
